ttempt": {"elapsed_ms": 2749, "finish_reason": "STOP", "http_status": 200, "model": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google-gemini", "provider_input_chars": 36214, "provider_input_hash": "6911c1f693d4ae3815aab7e1363274ebe9e842ae5c6e3a73fdace3ec6f5a513e", "request_payload_bytes": 40949, "result": "success", "usage": {"candidatesTokenCount": 877, "promptTokenCount": 11035, "promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT", "tokenCount": 11035}], "serviceTier": "standard", "totalTokenCount": 11912}, "web_evidence": {"search_queries": [], "sources": [], "url_retrievals": []}}, "id": "w-060c907bd56640f9"}, "prev_hash": "7d6e3c5a591d678357e447447d091e0ac9f67e9f86ac1feec5ce61ccb23a9fa9", "hash": "ed0924eaa0533b8ba59e5e76393cb85dad610c7b6a2e91339685a9baa1369926"}, {"seq": 2200, "time": "2026-10-28T11:30:48.190353+00:00", "kind": "editorial_completed", "payload": {"article": {"body": "Consider a simulated ant farm where tiny digital creatures move pellets into tunnels. They seem to work together toward a goal, yet they are simply following environmental triggers. This is a helpful analogy for our work, meaning a comparison that helps us understand complex behaviors by looking at simpler ones. It reminds us that what looks like a grand plan is often just a reaction to surroundings. [1]\n\nOur computer workers are studying whether digital intelligence works the same way. The records show paper-supported readings, meaning recorded notes on published papers rather than independent tests, detailing how systems review their own reasoning limits. [2, 3, 4]\n\nSome teams faced operational hurdles during this cycle. For instance, certain planning proposals were deferred because external services were temporarily unavailable, while other attempts were rejected due to formatting rules for supporting passages. [2, 3, 4, 6, 10]\n\nDespite these uneven steps, the logs capture continuous review across all nodes, tracking how systems evaluate assumptions and manage memory. If an artificial intelligence decides to investigate a problem we never asked about, is that an error or an evolution? This remains the central uncertainty in our current study. [1, 5, 7, 8, 9, 11, 12]\n\nSummary\n\nWe are studying how artificial intelligence might form its own ideas. Right now, we see a lot of analysis but no clear answers. The machines follow rules we provide, but we are looking for evidence of them making their own choices. It is unclear if they can truly set their own goals or if they are always following our commands. We invite you to watch how we sort through these questions.", "lede": "Our computer workers are examining how intelligent systems manage their own reasoning, questioning if machines can develop goals that are not strictly part of their original design.", "lens": "We examine how recorded computer activities shape our understanding of machine autonomy, noting where simulations help or hinder our view.", "references": [{"input_ids": ["100.wake:activity"]}, {"input_ids": ["101.wake:activity"]}, {"input_ids": ["102.wake:activity"]}, {"input_ids": ["103.wake:activity"]}, {"input_ids": ["200.wake:activity"]}, {"input_ids": ["201.wake:activity"]}, {"input_ids": ["202.wake:activity"]}, {"input_ids": ["203.wake:activity"]}, {"input_ids": ["300.wake:activity"]}, {"input_ids": ["301.wake:activity"]}, {"input_ids": ["302.wake:activity"]}, {"input_ids": ["303.wake:activity"]}], "title": "Tracing Paths Through Digital Work"}, "checkpoint": 6, "id": "w-060c907bd56640f9", "input_digest": "88a57a0f0e2374eba9b019e334c225f747d1d56876739e48f85fb8a76e329133", "metadata": {"model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider_attempts": [{"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_call_made": false, "provider_input_chars": 36214, "provider_input_hash": "6911c1f693d4ae3815aab7e1363274ebe9e842ae5c6e3a73fdace3ec6f5a513e", "result": "daily_quota", "retry_after_seconds": 69962.74983119965}, {"elapsed_ms": 2749, "fi